    "recommendations": "• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective address numbers visible from the road in both directions.\n• Trim vegetation along the front driveway to maintain clear sightlines and overhead clearance for emergency vehicles.\n• Keep a rear access gate unlocked or secured with a breakaway latch to allow responders to reach the back of the property without delay.\n• Mark any secondary access points with clearly visible signage so arriving responders can quickly identify all entry options.\n• Clear a direct walking path between the main residence and the detached structure so responders can move between buildings without obstruction.\n• Remove stored equipment or materials from in front of the detached structure to allow responders to approach and work around it freely.\n• Thin dense vegetation between the main residence and the detached structure so responders have an unobstructed line of sight between the two buildings.\n• Post the property address visibly at the detached structure if it has a separate entrance from the main driveway.\n• Keep the parking area clear enough that emergency vehicles can pull in and turn around without being blocked by parked vehicles.\n• Identify which fenced sections have gates and mark those gates so responding crews do not waste time searching for access points along the perimeter."
